# Public browser configuration only. Anything in a VITE_* variable ends up in the downloaded
# JavaScript, so never put secrets here. The frontend needs no Supabase keys at all: sign-in,
# codes and sessions go through the Stayblz API, which keeps tokens in HttpOnly cookies.

# Local development: leave blank to use Vite's /api proxy to http://localhost:4000.
# Production builds ignore it and call the same-origin /api proxy in vercel.json
# (https://stayblz-app.com/api → the Render API), so cookies stay first-party.
VITE_API_URL=

# STAYBLZ TV has no frontend variable on purpose. Its settings (TV_ON_AIR, TV_STREAM_URL, TV_TITLE,
# TV_NEXT_AT) live in the backend .env: a VITE_* stream address would be public and skip the paywall.
# The page reads /api/tv/status and the player gets the stream from /api/tv/playback.
# When a stream provider is chosen, add its host to connect-src and media-src in vercel.json.
